{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:44:01Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 16, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Give tasks a due date\n2\t\n3\t**Taiga:** #12\n4\t**Spec:** `docs/spec.md`\n5\t\n6\t*Note: this overwrites `docs/design.md` from the previous cycle (Taiga #11),\n7\tsame scratch-turnover reasoning as the spec.*\n8\t\n9\t## Conventions established\n10\t\n11\tReviewed `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, `App.jsx`,\n12\tand `frontend/src/App.css`. No component library \u2014 plain function\n13\tcomponents, plain CSS, native HTML form controls (`<select>`, `<input>`).\n14\tThe precedent this feature mirrors throughout is **priority**: a per-row\n15\tnative control, styled with a `-select`/`-input` class plus a state\n16\tmodifier class, changed directly from the row without an edit mode. Due\n17\tdate follows the same shape, using `<input type=\"date\">` in place of\n18\t`<select>`.\n19\t\n20\tOne useful fact confirmed directly, not assumed: Pydantic's default JSON\n21\tencoding of a `date` field is `YYYY-MM-DD`, which is exactly the value\n22\tformat `<input type=\"date\">` produces and consumes. So `task.due_date` can\n23\tbe bound to the input's `value` with no parsing/formatting step in either\n24\tdirection \u2014 same as every other field here, no new date library needed.\n25\t\n26\t## New elements\n27\t\n28\t1. **Due-date input** \u2014 `<input type=\"date\">`, styled as `.due-date-input`,\n29\t   sibling to `.priority-select` in both `AddTask` and each `TaskRow`.\n30\t2. **Clear control** \u2014 a small `\u00d7` button, shown only when a due date is\n31\t   set, because `<input type=\"date\">`'s native clear affordance is\n32\t   inconsistent across browsers (Firefox has none) and AC3 requires\n33\t   clearing to always be possible.\n34\t3. **Overdue badge** \u2014 `.overdue-badge`, a pill with an icon glyph *and* the\n35\t   text \"Overdue\" (AC4: not colour alone).\n36\t\n37\t## AddTask (`frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`)\n38\t\n39\tAdd a due-date input between the priority select and the Add button.\n40\tOptional \u2014 empty is a valid submission (AC1).\n41\t\n42\t```\n43\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n44\t\u2502 [ What needs doing?      ] [Normal \u25be] [ \ud83d\udcc5 mm/dd/yyyy ] [Add] \u2502\n45\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\t- New state: `const [dueDate, setDueDate] = useState('')`.\n49\t- `onAdd(trimmed, priority, dueDate || null)` \u2014 empty string becomes `null`,\n50\t  never sent as `\"\"`.\n51\t- Reset to `''` after submit, same lifecycle as `priority` resetting to\n52\t  `'normal'`.\n53\t- `aria-label=\"Due date (optional)\"` \u2014 the word \"optional\" in the label\n54\t  itself, since this is the one field on the form that isn't required and\n55\t  that should be discoverable without relying on a visual asterisk\n56\t  convention this app doesn't otherwise use.\n57\t- No clear button needed here \u2014 the field is empty by default and a user\n58\t  who typed a date can just retype it; the clear-affordance problem only\n59\t  matters for an *existing stored* value (row context, below).\n60\t\n61\t## TaskRow display state (`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`)\n62\t\n63\tDue date sits immediately after the priority select, followed by the clear\n64\tbutton (only when a value exists) and the overdue badge (only when\n65\toverdue). This is a direct, un-modal edit exactly like priority \u2014 no\n66\t\"Edit\" click required.\n67\t\n68\t**Populated, future due date, not overdue:**\n69\t```\n70\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n71\t\u2502 Buy groceries      [Normal \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-08-20] [\u00d7]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n72\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\t**Populated, overdue (past due, not done):**\n76\t```\n77\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n78\t\u2502 File taxes  [High \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-08-01] [\u00d7]  [\u26a0 Overdue]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n79\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t**No due date set (default/empty state for this field):**\n83\t```\n84\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n85\t\u2502 Water plants        [Low \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 dd/mm/yyyy]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n86\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n87\t```\n88\tNo clear button (nothing to clear) and no badge. The unset date input\n89\tshows the browser's own placeholder \u2014 no custom \"No due date\" text needed,\n90\tconsistent with the input being a live editable control, not a label.\n91\t\n92\t**Due date today (populated, not overdue \u2014 AC5):**\n93\tSame layout as \"future due date, not overdue\" above \u2014 no visual distinction\n94\tbetween \"due today\" and \"due in 10 days.\" The spec's AC5 only requires\n95\t*absence* of the overdue marking, not a separate \"due today\" treatment,\n96\tand adding one would be inventing a state the spec didn't ask for.\n97\t\n98\t**Overdue task marked done (AC7 \u2014 badge suppressed):**\n99\t```\n100\t\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n101\t\u2502 ~~Renew passport~~  [Normal \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-07-15] [\u00d7]        [Delete]     \u2502\n102\t\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n103\t```\n104\tStrikethrough/dim via the existing `.task.done .task-title` rule \u2014 due\n105\tdate input and clear button remain visible and editable (editing a done\n106\ttask's due date is not restricted by the spec), badge is gone because\n107\t`isOverdue()` is gated on `!task.done` (below).\n108\t\n109\t**Very long title + overdue badge together:** title uses the existing\n110\t`.task-title { flex: 1 }`, which already absorbs long text without pushing\n111\tfixed-width controls off-row; badge and date input keep their own\n112\tintrinsic width via `white-space: nowrap`. Adding `flex-wrap: wrap` to\n113\t`.task` (new, see CSS) lets the row wrap onto a second line on narrow\n114\tviewports instead of overflowing, since this row now carries more controls\n115\tthan the priority-only version did.\n116\t\n117\t## TaskRow editing state (title edit)\n118\t\n119\tUnchanged. Due date is edited independently of the title-edit mode, same\n120\tas priority already is \u2014 `isEditing` only ever covered the title `<input>`\n121\tand Save/Cancel, and stays that way.\n122\t\n123\t## Empty / Loading states\n124\t\n125\tNo change. Due date is a per-row field, not a filter or list mode \u2014 the\n126\tspec's non-goals explicitly exclude sorting/filtering by due date or\n127\toverdue status, so there is no \"no overdue tasks\" empty state and no\n128\tloading-state difference to design.\n129\t\n130\t## Error state\n131\t\n132\tNo new error UI. A rejected due-date change (network failure, or the\n133\tAC8 malformed-value case reachable only via direct API, not through this\n134\tdate-picker) surfaces through the existing `run()` \u2192 `setError(e.message)`\n135\t\u2192 `.error` banner path in `App.jsx`, identical to how a failed priority\n136\tchange already surfaces. The native `<input type=\"date\">` itself prevents\n137\tmalformed values from being typed through the UI at all, which is why AC8\n138\tis scoped to direct API use only.\n139\t\n140\t## Overdue logic (drives the badge, implemented in `TaskList.jsx`)\n141\t\n142\t```js\n143\tconst todayISO = () => new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-CA') // YYYY-MM-DD, local time\n144\tconst isOverdue = (task) => !task.done && task.due_date != null && task.due_date < todayISO()\n145\t```\n146\tString comparison is valid because both sides are `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 lexical\n147\torder matches chronological order for that format. `toLocaleDateString('en-CA')`\n148\tis used (not `toISOString()`) specifically to get the *local* calendar\n149\tdate, not UTC, so \"today\" matches what the user's own clock says \u2014 the\n150\tspec's \"server's local date\" scoping is about the stored value, not this\n151\tcomparison, which is a pure client-side same-day check against the\n152\tbrowser's own clock.\n153\t\n154\t## Component/prop wiring\n155\t\n156\t- `TaskList` gains an `onDueDateChange` prop, threaded to `TaskRow`,\n157\t  mirroring `onPriorityChange` exactly (`TaskList.jsx:15,32`).\n158\t- `App.jsx` gains `onDueDateChange={(id, dueDate) => run(() => api.setDueDate(id, dueDate))}`,\n159\t  passed to `TaskList`, mirroring `onPriorityChange` (`App.jsx:84`).\n160\t- `AddTask`'s `onAdd` signature grows a third argument; its one caller in\n161\t  `App.jsx:64` updates to `(title, priority, dueDate) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority, dueDate))`.\n162\t\n163\t## Styling (`frontend/src/App.css`)\n164\t\n165\tNew rules, placed after the existing `.priority-select` block (the nearest\n166\tprecedent):\n167\t\n168\t```css\n169\t.task { flex-wrap: wrap; }\n170\t\n171\t.due-date-input {\n172\t  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n173\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n174\t  border-radius: 5px;\n175\t  background: #fff;\n176\t  color: #16191c;\n177\t  font: inherit;\n178\t  font-size: 0.85rem;\n179\t}\n180\t\n181\t.due-date-clear {\n182\t  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n183\t  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n184\t  border-radius: 5px;\n185\t  background: #fff;\n186\t  color: #5a646c;\n187\t  font-size: 0.85rem;\n188\t  line-height: 1;\n189\t  cursor: pointer;\n190\t}\n191\t.due-date-clear:hover { background: #f0f2f3; }\n192\t\n193\t.overdue-badge {\n194\t  display: inline-flex;\n195\t  align-items: center;\n196\t  gap: 0.3rem;\n197\t  padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;\n198\t  border-radius: 999px;\n199\t  background: #fbe9e7;\n200\t  color: #a3271d;\n201\t  font-size: 0.8rem;\n202\t  font-weight: 600;\n203\t  white-space: nowrap;\n204\t}\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t`.due-date-input` and `.due-date-clear` match `.priority-select`'s exact\n208\tpadding/border/font-size (`App.css:96-104`) so all three per-row controls\n209\tread as one family at a glance \u2014 no new visual vocabulary introduced.\n210\t\n211\t`.overdue-badge` reuses the app's existing error palette\n212\t(`.error { color: #a3271d; background: #fbe9e7 }`, `App.css:79`) rather\n213\tthan inventing a new red, since \"overdue\" and \"error\" are the same\n214\tsemantic register (something needs attention) and this app already has\n215\texactly one red in its palette.\n216\t\n217\t**Contrast, computed:**\n218\t- `.overdue-badge` text `#a3271d` on its own background `#fbe9e7`:\n219\t  **6.25:1** (needs 4.5:1 for text \u2014 passes).\n220\t- `.overdue-badge` text `#a3271d` on the card background `#fff` (the badge\n221\t  sits inline on the white `.task` card): **7.33:1** \u2014 passes either way.\n222\t- `.due-date-clear` text `#5a646c` on `#fff`: **6.04:1** \u2014 passes.\n223\t\n224\t`#ccd2d6` borders on `.due-date-input`/`.due-date-clear` are the same\n225\tborder colour already used on every input/button/select in this app\n226\t(`App.css:14,18,98`); it measures ~1.53:1 against white, under the 3:1\n227\tnon-text guideline, but that's a pre-existing app-wide convention, not a\n228\tnew pairing introduced by this feature \u2014 out of scope to redesign here per\n229\tthe non-goals (no other affected-area line touches existing controls'\n230\tborders).\n231\t\n232\t## Accessibility\n233\t\n234\t- **Non-colour cue (AC4):** the badge's accessible name is the visible text\n235\t  \"Overdue\" \u2014 the `\u26a0` glyph is `aria-hidden=\"true\"` and purely decorative,\n236\t  so the requirement is met by text content, not by the icon or the colour.\n237\t- **Labels:** every new/changed control has an explicit `aria-label`:\n238\t  `\"Due date (optional)\"` (AddTask), `` `Due date for ${task.title}` ``\n239\t  (row), `` `Clear due date for ${task.title}` `` (clear button) \u2014 same\n240\t  pattern as the existing `` `Priority for ${task.title}` ``.\n241\t- **Focus order:** DOM order is title \u2192 priority \u2192 due date \u2192 clear (if\n242\t  present) \u2192 overdue badge (not focusable, it's `role=\"status\"`, not\n243\t  interactive) \u2192 Edit \u2192 Done \u2192 Delete. Tab order follows visual left-to-\n244\t  right order, consistent with the rest of the row.\n245\t- **Target size:** `.due-date-clear` uses the same padding as\n246\t  `.priority-select` (0.4rem 0.6rem) rather than a smaller icon-only\n247\t  button, keeping it at the same touch target size as every other per-row\n248\t  control \u2014 no new small-target element introduced.\n249\t- **Live update:** the badge's `role=\"status\"` means a due-date edit that\n250\t  causes a task to newly become (or stop being) overdue is announced to\n251\t  screen reader users without requiring focus to move, matching the\n252\t  existing `aria-live=\"polite\"` treatment already used for the empty-state\n253\t  message (`TaskList.jsx:21`).\n254\t\n255\t## Acceptance criteria \u2192 design traceability\n256\t\n257\t| AC | Design element |\n258\t|----|-----------------|\n259\t| 1 | AddTask due-date input defaults to `''` \u2192 sent as `null`; nothing required to submit. |\n260\t| 2 | AddTask due-date input value flows through `onAdd` \u2192 row displays it via `.due-date-input` bound to `task.due_date`. |\n261\t| 3 | Row `.due-date-input` (`onChange`) sets/changes; `.due-date-clear` (shown only when set) clears to `null`. |\n262\t| 4 | `.overdue-badge` \u2014 text \"Overdue\" + decorative icon, not colour-only; contrast computed above. |\n263\t| 5 | `isOverdue()` uses `<` (strict), so a due date equal to today's local date renders the \"future/not overdue\" row layout. |\n264\t| 6 | `isOverdue()` short-circuits `false` on `due_date == null`; future dates fail the `<` check. |\n265\t| 7 | `isOverdue()` is gated on `!task.done` \u2014 done-task wireframe above shows the badge absent regardless of stored date. |\n266\t| 8 | No UI path produces a malformed value \u2014 `<input type=\"date\">` constrains input; error, if any, surfaces via the existing `.error` banner. |\n267\t| 9 | No new design surface \u2014 persistence is a backend/store concern, not a rendering one. |\n268\t\n269\t## Out of scope (per spec non-goals, not redesigned here)\n270\t\n271\t- No due-date column/sort, no due-date filter chip alongside\n272\t  `TaskFilter`/`SearchTasks`.\n273\t- No time-of-day picker \u2014 `type=\"date\"` only.\n274\t- No \"due today\" distinct visual treatment (see AC5 wireframe note above).\n275\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01X6f8c5xJGQwBEvDf38g6ML", "session_id": "042a6643-a2fe-4545-9f8c-0399575d03bd"}}
